/// The project's CI on GitHub Actions, for any kind of app: go vet, the tests
/// (the runner has Docker, for testcontainers), the build, and a check that
/// the generated code is what the model generates (esquadro gen -check, with
/// the esquadro version of the lockfile). With docker, it builds the image
/// and, on tags v*, publishes it to GitHub's container registry
/// (ghcr.io/<owner>/<repo>).
blueprint github_actions {
  version "0.1.0"
  requires app
  optional docker
}
